LeetCode 257 — Binary Tree Paths
Problem Understanding

Given the root of a binary tree, return all root-to-leaf paths as strings.

For every path:

root → node → node → leaf

format it as:

value->value->value
Example
                1
              /   \
             2     3
              \
               5

The root-to-leaf paths are:

1 → 2 → 5
1 → 3

So the answer is:

["1->2->5", "1->3"]
First Important Observation

A path should end only at a leaf.

A leaf is:

root.left == null && root.right == null

So the traversal is:

Start at root
    ↓
keep building current path
    ↓
when leaf is reached
    ↓
add path to answer

This is naturally a DFS + backtracking problem.

Approaches

We'll go from:

Brute Force
   ↓
BFS with path stored in queue
   ↓
Recursive DFS with String
   ↓
DFS + StringBuilder + Backtracking

The last one is the most memory-efficient standard implementation.

Approach 1 — Brute Force: Store Complete Path at Every Node
Idea

At every node, maintain the complete path from root to that node.

For each child, create a new path list by copying the current one.

When we reach a leaf, save that path.

For example:

        1
       / \
      2   3
       \
        5

We maintain:

At 1 → [1]

At 2 → [1,2]

At 5 → [1,2,5]

At 3 → [1,3]

Then convert these lists to strings.

This is easy to understand, but copying the path at every node costs extra time and memory.

Code
import java.util.*;

class Solution {

    public List<String> binaryTreePaths(TreeNode root) {

        List<String> result = new ArrayList<>();

        if (root == null) {
            return result;
        }

        List<Integer> path = new ArrayList<>();
        dfs(root, path, result);

        return result;
    }

    private void dfs(
            TreeNode root,
            List<Integer> path,
            List<String> result) {

        if (root == null) {
            return;
        }

        // Create a new copy of the path
        List<Integer> currentPath = new ArrayList<>(path);
        currentPath.add(root.val);

        if (root.left == null && root.right == null) {

            StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();

            for (int i = 0; i < currentPath.size(); i++) {

                if (i > 0) {
                    sb.append("->");
                }

                sb.append(currentPath.get(i));
            }

            result.add(sb.toString());
            return;
        }

        dfs(root.left, currentPath, result);
        dfs(root.right, currentPath, result);
    }
}

